00:40:06,834 --> 00:40:10,508
as the gold or the ground truth token. And in this case,

607
00:40:10,524 --> 00:40:13,701
what happens then is that the text generation model actually,

608
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:18,258
the way it minimizes this loss is that, okay, it receives the token y0 at

609
00:40:18,758 --> 00:40:21,676
timestep 0. What it actually does is that it generates,

610
00:40:22,318 --> 00:40:25,222
it actually knows what the, like at the time of training,

611
00:40:25,447 --> 00:40:28,143
and this is why we call it as teacher forcing. At the time of training,

612
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:31,788
what it does is that it knows what the next

613
00:40:32,288 --> 00:40:35,962
prediction is, which is it knows the gold prediction. And what we do is we

614
00:40:36,462 --> 00:40:40,555
train this model to minimize the loss here,

615
00:40:40,779 --> 00:40:45,404
which is the negative log likelihood of actually generating— actually

616
00:40:45,436 --> 00:40:47,812
observing this specific token,

617
00:40:48,647 --> 00:40:52,035
the correct token y1* given the token y0*.

618
00:40:52,742 --> 00:40:56,950
Then at next time, what we do is we actually perform the

619
00:40:57,176 --> 00:41:01,903
same step, but we right now, instead of just generating y1*

620
00:41:02,097 --> 00:41:05,863
given one previous token y0*, what we do is we now minimize

621
00:41:07,414 --> 00:41:11,668
the log likelihood of actually generating y2* given

622
00:41:12,283 --> 00:41:15,599
both y0* and y1* as input

623
00:41:16,099 --> 00:41:19,307
context. And this keeps on going where we do the same

624
00:41:19,807 --> 00:41:24,523
thing when we have y3* as the goal label. Then we minimize the

625
00:41:24,652 --> 00:41:28,447
log probability of observing this specific

626
00:41:28,479 --> 00:41:31,079
token given all 3 input tokens that we have seen previously.

627
00:41:32,048 --> 00:41:36,164
And how it can be more formalized in a more tight

628
00:41:36,197 --> 00:41:39,746
notation is that where we just sum over all possible tokens

629
00:41:40,246 --> 00:41:43,596
that we have seen, where we actually minimize these

630
00:41:43,709 --> 00:41:46,912
individual token log probabilities

631
00:41:46,944 --> 00:41:49,339
given the previous input context that we have seen.

632
00:41:52,517 --> 00:41:56,814
So, and again, as you can see, is that we are kind of somehow forcing

633
00:41:56,927 --> 00:42:01,385
the model to actually mimic what

634
00:42:01,885 --> 00:42:05,403
we have actually seen. I mean, it's basically forcing the model to generate

635
00:42:05,903 --> 00:42:09,404
the token that comes next in our gold

636
00:42:09,904 --> 00:42:12,121
data, right? And the gold data is basically all the data that we find on

637
00:42:12,219 --> 00:42:16,141
the internet. And this algorithm is also known as teacher forcing.

638
00:42:16,734 --> 00:42:20,884
I mean, you have seen this already. Again, as I said, right, in a model-specific,

639
00:42:20,965 --> 00:42:24,266
architectural-specific way, we looked at how we train LSTMs using this.

640
00:42:24,907 --> 00:42:28,913
We looked at how we train Transformers using this similar objective. But just trying

641
00:42:29,413 --> 00:42:33,688
to abstract that this teacher forcing algorithm is the same thing that we apply when

642
00:42:33,785 --> 00:42:37,807
we are training any specific language model, right? So the pretraining

643
00:42:37,823 --> 00:42:39,890
step is literally done using this objective.

644
00:42:42,068 --> 00:42:45,619
OK, so I'd quickly like to wrap up what we saw so far

645
00:42:45,812 --> 00:42:49,042
is that, again, looking at this model-agnostic way of talking about

646
00:42:49,542 --> 00:42:52,790
text generation is that we basically say that

647
00:42:53,386 --> 00:42:56,897
the decoding is always

648
00:42:57,107 --> 00:43:01,348
autoregressive. The way we actually generate text from a model is that

649
00:43:01,848 --> 00:43:05,558
the model generates one token at a time using the context and

650
00:43:05,574 --> 00:43:08,833
the previous generated tokens as inputs. For generating the next token.

651
00:43:09,366 --> 00:43:12,533
And then what the model does is actually generates a set

652
00:43:13,033 --> 00:43:16,425
of scores for each token in the vocabulary. And then we convert it into a

653
00:43:16,925 --> 00:43:21,396
probability distribution using the softmax function. And what

654
00:43:21,896 --> 00:43:25,012
we can say is that the decoding step doesn't have to care about whether

655
00:43:25,368 --> 00:43:28,849
the distribution that you get at each step is calibrated or not,

656
00:43:29,157 --> 00:43:32,572
because that's actually what's done using this maximum likelihood

657
00:43:33,072 --> 00:43:36,668
estimation objective. When we actually use this to train the model to predict the next

658
00:43:36,717 --> 00:43:39,799
token over a dataset of sequences that we have already seen.

659
00:43:40,827 --> 00:43:45,066
So with this, again, we have defined our model-agnostic way of how a

660
00:43:45,566 --> 00:43:49,321
text generation model is trained. And then we basically see how we

661
00:43:49,821 --> 00:43:53,496
perform decoding, right? So as I said, right, so the

662
00:43:53,996 --> 00:43:57,173
goal of the decoding is to actually give you a token out of a probability

663
00:43:57,189 --> 00:44:00,883
distribution, right? So what you can see is that This is your text generation model

664
00:44:01,383 --> 00:44:04,643
that you have trained using the MLE objective. And what you have done is then

665
00:44:04,900 --> 00:44:08,145
taken this probability— obtained this probability distribution from the score

666
00:44:08,645 --> 00:44:11,985
of vectors that you get from this model. And eventually, the decoding function gives you

667
00:44:12,018 --> 00:44:14,614
one token from this probability distribution.

668
00:44:15,720 --> 00:44:19,195
So then— and what keeps happening is

669
00:44:19,292 --> 00:44:24,159
that what you can see is here

670
00:44:24,659 --> 00:44:27,008
what I was previously saying, that to make sure that these things work well in

671
00:44:27,508 --> 00:44:31,186
an autoregressive manner, is that from this score, you actually get a token and

672
00:44:31,202 --> 00:44:36,276
you pass it along. And you keep doing that until unless you have actually obtained

673
00:44:36,645 --> 00:44:40,435
the end of sequence on which, you know, when the

674
